On Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:10:51 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:
>
>> To your question about more than one level: local patches already
>> reach any level, since files/patch-* paths are relative to WRKSRC
>> and can name vendor/... or a tuple's directory. Upstream patches for
>> several different trees cannot share one -d, and ports that have them
>> call ${PATCH} -d per tree in post-patch, as editors/textadept does
>> for scintilla, lua, cdk, and termkey.
>
> In that case I would prefer to use post-patch then. Again setting these
> Makefile-level variables are blunt instruments, and we are doing a
> highly targeted patch of a dependency. That should be crystal clear in
> the Makefile.

Done in "[freebsd-ports PATCH v10] net-mgmt/signoz: Observability
platform for logs, metrics, and traces" [1]. The port no longer sets
PATCH_WRKSRC, PATCH_DIST_ARGS, PATCH_SITES, or PATCHFILES. The patch
is one line in post-patch, next to the other source edits:

    ${PATCH} -d ${WRKSRC_sonic} -p1 < ${DISTDIR}/${DIST_SUBDIR}/${SONIC_PATCH}

The commit is still fetched from GitHub and checksummed in distinfo,
as you asked in the v1 thread [2]. It cannot stay in PATCHFILES,
because do-patch would apply it to WRKSRC before post-patch runs. So
it is a distfile in its own :sonic_patch group, and EXTRACT_ONLY keeps
it out of extraction. sysutils/osquery fetches an upstream GitHub
commit the same way, a :patches group left out of EXTRACT_ONLY.
SONIC_PATCH sits beside the sonic GH_TUPLE with the comment saying
what the fix is, so the dependency, its version, and its patch read
together.

That needs one Makefile-level variable, EXTRACT_ONLY. The port must
set it because go.mk's default extracts every DISTFILES entry except
the .mod file. The other choice is to commit the upstream patch into
files/ under a name do-patch skips, as databases/mongodb80 does, and
drop EXTRACT_ONLY. That would undo the v1 decision to fetch the
commit, so I did not take it. Say if you would rather have it.

I ran makesum and a clean extract and patch. All five distfiles pass
their checksums, the commit is not extracted, and post-patch applies
it to sonic-1.15.4, so loader/mmap_unix.go passes ^uintptr(0) as the
fd. portclippy, portfmt, and portlint are clean. The v10 notes carry
the interdiff against v9.

Still open for you: v10 has not been built, since it changes only the
fetch, extract, and patch phases, and I ran those. It needs your
poudriere testport on amd64 and aarch64. My questions about the
prebuilt web frontend and the /usr/local/etc/signoz layout also have
no answer yet [3].

